  "metaDescription": "Search teams recovered additional remains at the burnt PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory as authorities initiate an investigation into potential negligence.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Search and rescue teams have recovered additional remains from the site of the fire at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory in Cikande.",
    "Authorities have elevated the case to a formal investigation, with inquiries focusing on potential corporate negligence and limited evacuation access.",
    "The Ministry of Manpower has committed to ensuring that all victims and their families receive appropriate severance pay and compensation."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire recently occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy manufacturing facility located in Cikande, Serang. Search and rescue operations are ongoing, with emergency teams discovering remains, some of which were located near emergency staircases that served as exit routes. Following the disaster, the Ministry of Manpower has launched an investigation to determine if the company failed to meet safety standards. Concerns have been raised regarding the adequacy of existing emergency evacuation infrastructure. In response to the high casualty rate and reported missing personnel, police have interviewed 19 witnesses to assist in the formal investigation. The government has pledged to ensure that victims and their families are provided with necessary financial support, including severance payments and death benefits through BPJS Ketenagakerjaan. Identification processes for the recovered remains are being conducted by disaster victim identification units at the Bhayangkara Hospital.",
